      "side": 1,
      "message": "I continue to find this really difficult to follow. In particular the lifecycle of the automatic keepalive is really not clear.\n\nIIUC, the general architecture here is that you want to have the AutomaticOnOffKeepalive object as something higher-level that manages the lifecycle of the underlying KeepaliveInfo. In principle I think this is a pretty good idea, but the way it\u0027s implemented in the latest patchset makes it really hard to understand.\n\nOne thing you could do is extract the AutomaticOnOffKeepalive class as a separate class, which would have methods to manage its own lifecycle. It would own a KI, it would know if automatic is on or off for that KI, if off it would behave like before, and if on, it would turn on the alarm as it starts and turn off the alarm as it stops, and then you have the temp stop event completely separate at the level above KeepaliveInfo, and you would need essentially no changes at all in KeepaliveInfo (you would no longer have the TEMP_DISABLED reason, because it would be a the upper level). I think it\u0027s probably not too hard to get there from what you have here.",
      "revId": "8b7c753d51ab74f0876ef4e7757192fb48470a21",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
